		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=15924&amp;sid=5cce3abb7a0c72e9100ea8178f696f01#15924"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Sun Sep 08, 2002 6:28 am<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=15924&amp;sid=5cce3abb7a0c72e9100ea8178f696f01"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Nicholi looks at his friend's straight face as he takes the note and reads it.  He absently pulls a pencil from a pocket and chews it while reading.  When he reaches the last sentence he quickly places an apostrophe in &quot;its&quot; making it &quot;it's&quot;.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
The cleric glances for a moment at the drawing then turns the note over to look at the back for anything else marked on it.  He wonders for a moment at the tack holes in the paper.  He hands the note back to his friend, casting a chastising glance at the giggling ladies, and looks directly at him.  &quot;Lanturias, although I don't see the need for this, it is your choice.  If you have thought this through and feel you must, then I suggest you re-write it and leave out the parts about clipping your nails.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;And perhaps you should slow down on the drink.  It will dull your wits for when this blue-eyed female does come for a visit.  You would like to have a clear mind to enjoy her beauty and conversation correct?&quot; 
<br />
<i></i></span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
