				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Lanturias nods in response to Nicholi, and then stands. &quot;I think I shall retire for the evening, all. It was a pleasure meeting you Mechaela, and I was honored by the pleasant  company of both you and Arialana. Arialana, keep your feet dry.&quot; Lanturias grins at her and then holds out his hand for Nicholi to shake. &quot;If I don't see you before the play in Freeport, just leave me a note as to where I should meet you. Take care of yourself, Nicholi.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
As Lanturias leaves the table he murmurs quietly &quot;May Tunare watch over you all.&quot; 
